sea-regime-gibraltar = No passage treaty in 1925; transit passage under the UN Law of the Sea from 1994.
sea-regime-dover = Transit passage under the UN Law of the Sea from 1994.
sea-regime-oresund = Copenhagen Convention of 1857: free to commercial shipping, silent on warships and war.
sea-regime-great_belt = Copenhagen Convention of 1857, as the Øresund; Danish territorial waters.
sea-regime-kiel_canal = Treaty of Versailles, arts. 380–386: open to ships of nations at peace with Germany.
sea-regime-messina = Italian territorial waters; no passage treaty.
sea-regime-otranto = No passage treaty; transit passage under the UN Law of the Sea from 1994.
sea-regime-corinth_canal = Greek national canal, no treaty.
sea-regime-dardanelles = Lausanne Straits Convention (1923): free passage; Turkey may stop only enemy ships when at war. Montreux from 1936.
sea-regime-bosporus = Lausanne Straits Convention (1923), then Montreux (1936), as the Dardanelles.
sea-regime-kerch = No treaty in 1925; a Russia–Ukraine agreement of 2003 (denounced in 2023).
sea-regime-suez_canal = Convention of Constantinople (1888): passage in war and peace; British reserved points of 1922.
sea-regime-bab_el_mandeb = No passage treaty; transit passage under the UN Law of the Sea from 1994.
sea-regime-hormuz = No passage treaty; transit passage under the UN Law of the Sea, contested by Iran and Oman.
sea-regime-malacca = No passage treaty; transit passage under the UN Law of the Sea from 1994.
sea-regime-sunda = No passage treaty.
sea-regime-lombok = No passage treaty.
sea-regime-tsushima = No passage treaty.
sea-regime-tsugaru = No passage treaty.
sea-regime-la_perouse = No passage treaty.
sea-regime-tatar = No passage treaty.
sea-regime-bering = No passage treaty.
sea-regime-magellan = Chile–Argentina Boundary Treaty of 1881: neutral for ever, free to all flags, no fortifications.
sea-regime-panama_canal = Hay–Bunau-Varilla Treaty (1903): Canal Zone under US control; Torrijos–Carter (1977) hands it to Panama in 1999.
